WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.827
My parents have trouble reading small print.

00:00:03.867 --> 00:00:07.693
Suniye is an Android app built for them.

00:00:07.733 --> 00:00:11.560
It reads text from photos and PDFs in Hindi.

00:00:11.600 --> 00:00:14.682
This is a synthetic practice photo.

00:00:14.722 --> 00:00:17.805
Share it to Suniye. The phone recognizes its text,

00:00:17.845 --> 00:00:20.927
then the app reads it aloud in Hindi.

00:00:20.967 --> 00:00:28.260
App reading: “Namaste” (Hello).

00:00:28.300 --> 00:00:32.144
Now open a two-page PDF.

00:00:32.184 --> 00:00:36.027
Listen to page one, then tap Next page.

00:00:36.067 --> 00:00:45.527
App reading: “Bill”.

00:00:45.567 --> 00:00:47.527
Exact second-page source: “Thank you”.

00:00:47.567 --> 00:00:54.227
App reading: “Dhanyavaad” (Thank you).

00:00:54.267 --> 00:01:00.382
Repeat plays the same recording; Slow reduces its speed.

00:01:00.422 --> 00:01:06.537
Stop stays at the bottom. The original remains available.

00:01:06.577 --> 00:01:10.615
In WhatsApp, open the photo or PDF.

00:01:10.655 --> 00:01:14.692
Choose Share, then Suniye. A caregiver sets it up first.

00:01:14.732 --> 00:01:18.770
Testing on my parents’ actual phones is still pending.

00:01:18.810 --> 00:01:20.270
Try the pilot with a caregiver.

00:01:20.310 --> 00:01:21.770
suniye-reader.onrender.com
